API Reporter and Ansible release strategy

After the Merge Request is approved and merged into develop, manage two independent releases:

the API Reporter RPM release
the Ansible/REX release

They do not need to use the same version number.

Phase 1 — Merge into develop

Once approvals are complete:

1. Merge the MR into: develop
2. Wait for the develop pipeline to finish.
3. Confirm that all required build jobs are green.

At this point, the source code, RPM module, and Ansible integration are present on develop, but this does not necessarily mean both release artifacts have already been published.

Phase 2 — Release the API Reporter RPM

The Reporter RPM uses tags such as: m50-api-reporter-rpm-v3.0.0
The GitLab rules already recognize this pattern: m50-api-reporter-rpm-v<version>

Step 1 — Update your local develop
After the MR is merged:
git checkout develop
git pull origin develop
Confirm that you are on the correct commit:
git status
git log --oneline -5
The working tree should be clean.

Step 2 — Check existing Reporter tags
git tag --list "m50-api-reporter-rpm-v*" --sort=-v:refname | head -10
If the latest tag is: m50-api-reporter-rpm-v3.0.1 or: m50-api-reporter-rpm-v3.1.0
However, if the pipeline derives the RPM release number independently, the tag may remain at an application version while the RPM filename increments its release number.

Step 3 — Create the Reporter release tag
Example:
git tag m50-api-reporter-rpm-v3.0.1
Verify it:
git show m50-api-reporter-rpm-v3.0.1 --no-patch
Push it:
git push origin m50-api-reporter-rpm-v3.0.1
This should trigger the Reporter RPM release pipeline.

Step 4 — Validate the Reporter pipeline
Verify that the jobs run successfully, especially:
build-m50-api-reporter-rpm
publish-m50-api-reporter-rpm
Open the build or publish log and identify the exact generated RPM filename, for example:
m50-api-reporter-3.0.0-9.el7.ubs.noarch.rpm
The important Ansible version value is the part before .noarch.rpm:
3.0.0-9.el7.ubs
Also verify that the RPM is available in the YUM repository used by the RCM Ansible role.

Phase 3 — Align the Ansible inventory version
The Ansible inventories currently contain something like: api_reporter_version: 3.0.0-8.el7.ubs
Compare that value with the RPM that was actually published.

If the new RPM is still version 8
No inventory update is needed: api_reporter_version: 3.0.0-8.el7.ubs

If the new RPM is version 9
Update all three inventory files:
scmt-rex-ansible/src/main/ansible/inventories/dev/CX/group_vars/rcm.yml
scmt-rex-ansible/src/main/ansible/inventories/te2/R0/group_vars/rcm.yml
scmt-rex-ansible/src/main/ansible/inventories/prd/P0/group_vars/rcm.yml

Change:
api_reporter_version: 3.0.0-8.el7.ubs to api_reporter_version: 3.0.0-9.el7.ubs

Validate:
git grep -n "api_reporter_version"
git diff --check
git diff

Then commit and push:
git add \
  scmt-rex-ansible/src/main/ansible/inventories/dev/CX/group_vars/rcm.yml \
  scmt-rex-ansible/src/main/ansible/inventories/te2/R0/group_vars/rcm.yml \
  scmt-rex-ansible/src/main/ansible/inventories/prd/P0/group_vars/rcm.yml

git commit -m "issue-6446: Update API Reporter RPM version for deployment"
git push origin develop

Direct pushes to develop may be blocked. In that case, create a small follow-up branch and MR instead.

The critical rule is:
api_reporter_version
must exactly match the RPM version published in the YUM repository.

Phase 4 — Release Ansible for REX
After the Ansible code and final Reporter RPM version are present on develop, create a new Ansible release.
The existing Ansible tags follow this pattern:
m50-ansible-v3.0.0.66
m50-ansible-v3.0.0.65

Step 1 — Update local develop
git checkout develop
git pull origin develop
git status

The working tree must be clean.

Step 2 — Find the latest Ansible release tag

git tag --list "m50-ansible-v*" --sort=-v:refname | head -10
If the latest tag is:
m50-ansible-v3.0.0.66
the next release would normally be: m50-ansible-v3.0.0.67

Step 3 — Create the Ansible tag from develop
git tag m50-ansible-v3.0.0.67
Verify the tag points to the intended develop commit:
git show m50-ansible-v3.0.0.67 --no-patch
Then push it:
git push origin m50-ansible-v3.0.0.67
This tag should trigger the Ansible release pipeline.

Step 4 — Validate the Ansible release
Confirm that the pipeline:

builds the Ansible artifact;
publishes it successfully;
makes the new version available to REX.

The Reporter RPM and the Ansible release can therefore look like:

Reporter RPM:
m50-api-reporter-3.0.0-9.el7.ubs.noarch.rpm
Ansible release:
m50-ansible-v3.0.0.67

These versions are intentionally independent.

Phase 5 — Deploy through REX
Once both releases are available:

1. Open REX.
2. Select the new Ansible release, for example:
  m50-ansible-v3.0.0.67
3. Select the TE2 environment.
4. Use the RCM target or limit, according to the existing REX configuration: RCM
5. Review the target hosts carefully. It should include the intended RCM servers, typically RCM1 and RCM2.
6. Start the deployment.

The RCM role will evaluate this task:
- name: Install API Reporter Package
  yum:
    name:
      - "m50-api-reporter-{{ api_reporter_version }}.noarch"
    state: present

Expected behavior:
- package absent → installed;
- different configured version → upgraded or downgraded;
- exact version already installed → task returns ok, with no package transaction.

Phase 6 — Validate on RCM servers
After REX completes, verify on each RCM server.
RPM
rpm -qa | grep m50-api-reporter
Expected example: m50-api-reporter-3.0.0-9.el7.ubs.noarch
Service
systemctl status api-reporter.service

Also:
systemctl is-enabled api-reporter.service
systemctl is-active api-reporter.service

Expected:
enabled
active

Local health check
curl -i http://127.0.0.1:8000/health

Local Reporter endpoint
curl -i http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/reporter

Through Apache/load balancer
https://fcscmt-actone-uat-ch.appl.ubs.net/reporter/health
and: 
https://fcscmt-actone-uat-ch.appl.ubs.net/reporter/api/reporter

Also validate the Excel endpoint.

Complete release order
1. MR approved
2. Merge into develop
3. Create API Reporter RPM tag from develop
4. Build and publish Reporter RPM
5. Confirm exact RPM version
6. Update api_reporter_version if necessary
7. Merge the version adjustment into develop
8. Create the next m50-ansible tag from develop
9. Build and publish the Ansible release
10. Select the new Ansible release in REX
11. Deploy with RCM limit
12. Validate RPM, service and endpoints on RCM1 and RCM2

The key principle is: release the Reporter RPM first, confirm its exact version, and only then release Ansible with an inventory that references that published RPM version




